  "fail": [
    {
      "name": "scifi-city-base",
      "problems": "At 1x the roofs, rooftop fixtures and alley speckle merge into a busy grey-green field; at 4x/8x the irregular roof outlines have lumpy single-pixel notches and muddled roof/wall junctions, especially the branching buildings and hollow round building. There is no clearly readable plaza to give the dense city breathing room. Simplify roof silhouettes and their interior texture into clean clusters, reserve a few larger quiet plaza/green-strip areas, and reduce incidental alley highlights. The ring-and-branch building group is conspicuous in the 3x3 repeat; reduce its contrast and distribute the larger roof masses less evenly. Keep the continuous wrap and restrained neon."
    },
    {
      "name": "scifi-city@winter-base",
      "problems": "The summer roof-shape/readability problem remains, and snow becomes a bright broken outline around almost every rooftop. At 1x the 3x3 repeat reads as white loops and speckle over near-black alleys; in the sparse tower composite these roof rims compete with the standing landmarks. Replace the all-over rim treatment with broader, quieter snow clusters on selected horizontal roof planes, retain exposed roof planes, reduce tiny bright edge flecks, and simplify the branching roof shapes. Keep the dark streets and actual summer layout."
    },
    {
      "name": "scifi-city@winter-tower-3",
      "problems": "Seasonal geometry changes: the summer tall left tower has a rooftop antenna reaching native y=10, but the winter drawing removes that antenna entirely (topmost pixel y=15 is snow). The anchored seasonal pair visibly loses its spire rather than gaining snow. Restore the antenna at the summer coordinates and height, keeping snow on the roof below it; do not move the foot or the two tower bodies."
    },
    {
      "name": "scifi-city@winter-tower-5",
      "problems": "Seasonal geometry changes: the tall cyan/magenta-tipped antenna above the summer observation deck starts at native y=10; winter truncates it to y=19 and loses the lit upper segment. This makes the same landmark visibly shorter when the season changes, as the registered 1x/4x/8x pair shows. Restore the full mast and its upper light pattern at the summer coordinates, adding snow only to the deck and supporting ledges."
    },
    {
      "name": "scifi-industry@winter-base",
      "problems": "Tanks, sheds and pipes remain recognizable, but snow makes nearly every pipe run and roof edge a similarly bright thin line. In the 1x 3x3 and sparse-stack proofs this becomes a dense circuit-like mesh, and narrow landmark supports disappear into the ground detail. At 4x/8x many snow marks are tiny disconnected-looking flecks rather than substantial deposits. Reduce snow contrast/coverage on minor pipework, group roof snow into fewer broad patches, and create quieter dark yard areas around the bright tank and shed masses. Preserve the readable summer machinery and dark streets."
    },
    {
      "name": "scifi-slums-base",
      "problems": "The shacks are dense enough and the alleys are irregular, but almost every roof and frontage has equally busy one-pixel corrugation, mottling or glints. At 1x this becomes a uniform gritty shimmer; at 4x/8x roof edges and patched surfaces are much less cleanly clustered than the approved slums/paddies. Consolidate the tiny marks into a few deliberate seams and broad tarp/metal patches per shack, simplify the darkest facade clutter, and leave quiet connected alley runs so individual packed shacks remain legible. Preserve the packed density and crooked layout."
    },
    {
      "name": "scifi-slums@winter-base",
      "problems": "The already busy summer roof/frontage texture is amplified by small white and cyan snow fragments on nearly every shack. The 1x repeated district becomes high-contrast salt-and-pepper texture rather than readable snow-covered shacks; the 4x/8x proof shows broken bright roof contours and scattered tiny highlights throughout the alleys. Group snow into continuous roof-plane patches of varied coverage, remove isolated bright clutter marks, and keep more broad exposed tarp/metal areas and quieter dark alleys. Do not lighten all edges equally."
    }
  ]
